Dear Listing Officer,

 

I write to request urgent listing of my Judicial Review claim Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Justice & HMCTS, for which the full N461 bundle was filed earlier today.

 

I am a vulnerable litigant in person, and I attach the signed medical report from my treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, confirming:
I am in a state of acute psychiatric risk,
the stress arising from administrative uncertainty is materially worsening my condition,
and that urgent judicial consideration is clinically necessary to prevent further deterioration.
 

Dr Hayse explicitly states that hospital admission may be required if this matter is not addressed promptly.

 

Given the medical urgency, the disability-related risks, and the fact that the N461 claim and N463 urgent application are now fully filed, I respectfully request that this matter is:
Referred immediately to the urgent judge, and
Given an expedited listing, as sought in Section 3 of the N463 form.
 

I would be grateful for confirmation that the Listing Office has received this escalation and that the matter is now with a judge.

 

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

 


--B_3852820736_94069743
